  "name": "Mannequin or flat-lay clothing photo to on-model product clip with Sisif",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ff180106-1fec-4cc7-b488-8ac729f11aff",
      "name": "Setup Instructions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1500,
        -700
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Turn mannequin or flat-lay clothing photos into on-model product clips with Sisif\n\n### Who it's for\nFashion brands, resellers and marketplace sellers who shoot garments on a mannequin or flat-lay and want an on-model motion clip for each item, at $1 per 5-second clip.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Google Drive Trigger** watches a folder for new files.\n2. Non-image files are ignored.\n3. The photo is downloaded and converted to a base64 data URL.\n4. **Sisif** animates it with an apparel prompt that puts the garment on a model (5-second portrait MP4).\n5. The workflow polls every 30 s until the clip is `READY`, `ERROR` or `REFUNDED`, for at most 40 checks.\n6. A row with the file name, Sisif video ID, status, video URL and any error is appended to Google Sheets (status `TIMEOUT` if it never finished).\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a Sisif API key at https://sisif.ai/users/api-keys/ and add it in n8n as a **Bearer Auth** credential. Select it on **Generate On-Model Clip** and **Check Video Status**.\n2. Add a Google Drive credential, then pick the folder to watch in **Google Drive Trigger**.\n3. Create a Google Sheet with the headers: `file_name`, `drive_file_id`, `sisif_video_id`, `status`, `video_url`, `poster_url`, `error_message`, `processed_at`. Select it in both Sheets nodes.\n4. Optionally edit the prompt in **Apparel Prompt Config**.\n5. Drop a test photo into the folder, check the row, then activate.\n\n### Customize\n- Change model look, setting or movement in **Apparel Prompt Config**.\n- Change the poll interval in **Wait 30s**."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "05b93149-eed8-4147-bf33-7d8eb5309e2b",
      "name": "Note: Prompt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -420,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "### Apparel prompt\nEdit `apparel_prompt` in **Apparel Prompt Config**. Describe the model, pose, setting and camera move. Keep the garment's color, pattern and details unchanged."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "851a1798-ba9c-42ff-a939-9fcfbd73db54",
      "name": "Note: Render Loop",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        380,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 880,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "### Sisif render loop\nThe photo is sent in `image` as a base64 data URL (`data:image/...;base64,...`). Sisif fixes duration and resolution for photo clips. The loop checks `/api/videos/{id}/status/` every 30 s: `READY` writes a success row, `ERROR`/`REFUNDED` writes a failure row with Sisif's `error_message` (failed renders return the credits), and after 40 checks it writes a `TIMEOUT` row."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9a5d9348-8dba-4c23-9d4a-a53187a87aa5",
      "name": "Google Drive Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDriveTrigger",
      "position": [
        -840,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "event": "fileCreated",
        "options": {},
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyMinute"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggerOn": "specificFolder",
        "folderToWatch": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "googleDriveOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "",
          "name": "Google Drive account"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7a09631a-6238-4c5f-b918-52a02084b63d",
      "name": "Is Image File?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
